WHERE vs HAVING?
WHERE filters rows BEFORE grouping. Works on normal columns.
HAVING filters groups AFTER grouping. Works on COUNT(), SUM() etc.

```sql
SELECT * FROM pgs WHERE rent > 8000;
SELECT city, COUNT(*) FROM pgs GROUP BY city HAVING COUNT(*) > 5;
GROUP BY purpose?

To group same values together for calculation.sqlSELECT city, COUNT(*) FROM pgs GROUP BY city;
-- Bangalore - 60, Hyderabad - 40
