What is a foreign key?
Foreign Key is a column in one table that refers to Primary Key of another table. It connects two tables.
pgs(pg_id) -> Primary Key
tenants(pg_id) -> Foreign Key
15. What is Referential Integrity?
Rule: You cannot add fake Foreign Key value. Value must exist in parent table. You cannot insert tenant with pg_id=999 if 999 PG does not exist. Database will block.
16. What is UNIQUE?
UNIQUE means no duplicate values in that column. UNIQUE can have 1 NULL, Primary Key cannot have NULL.
17. Can a table have multiple UNIQUE constraints?
YES. A table can have many UNIQUE columns.sqlCREATE TABLE tenants (
  email VARCHAR(100) UNIQUE,
  phone VARCHAR(10) UNIQUE
);
18. Can a table have multiple Primary Keys?
NO. Only ONE primary key allowed. But ONE primary key can be made of 2 columns - Composite Key.sqlPRIMARY KEY (pg_id, bed_no)19. Why use Aliases?
